course: dictionary
lesson: 16028
title: What is ventilation?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ventilation means fresh air moving into a room or building, and stale air moving out. Stale air is old, used air that feels stuffy.
explain: The vents and fans that move the air are called a ventilation system. «The classroom has good ventilation, so the air never feels stuffy.» Open windows and working fans both help.
explain: «Poor ventilation» means the air is not moving enough, so stale air, germs and fumes can build up. Good ventilation keeps us healthy.
fact: Ventilation means the movement of fresh air into a room and stale air out.
fact: A ventilation system uses vents or fans to move the air.
fact: «Good ventilation» helps stop germs spreading around a room.
fact: «Good ventilation» also removes fumes, so use paint or glue only where there is good ventilation.
fact: Never block the air vents near a heater.
exercise: «The room needs good ventilation, so open the window.» What does ventilation mean here? | Heat from a fire | A type of paint for walls | A loud noise from the street | *Fresh air moving in and stale air moving out
exercise: Which of these is a ventilation system? | A bedroom door | *A fan that moves air through a room | A rug on the floor | A bag of cold water
exercise: «Dad painted the shed with the door wide open for good ventilation.» Why is good ventilation important when painting? | It keeps the shed warm | It makes the paint dry more slowly and smudgy | It makes the paint smell stronger | *It removes fumes so the air stays safe to breathe
test: What does «poor ventilation» mean in a classroom? | *Not enough air moving, so stale air and germs can build up | Lots of fresh air moving in | The walls are freshly painted | The room is very bright
test: Why should you never block the air vents near a heater? | It makes the heater work faster forever | It makes the room smell of flowers | It makes the vents louder | *It stops air moving, which can be unsafe
exam: Which best describes ventilation? | Painting the walls of a building | *Moving fresh air into a room and stale air out | A kind of loud sound | A way of making a room darker
